Z||000000||TalShino||07-04-2000||08:41 AM||||Can I use the wiring harness from a 2.8l Fiero on a 3.0l v6 from a Buick Century that I have, that I wanna put in my 88 Coupe? If you're wondering why I'm going for a 3.0l.. it only cost 200$ for the whole car.. and I am tight on money! Hehe<P><BR>Sweet88Fiero &lt;-&gt; TalShino||||reg||5
Z||000001||TalShino||07-04-2000||08:55 AM||||Could someone inform me as to how I can juice more hp from that motor?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe.. I can stickers if needed<P><P>------------------<BR>Ray &lt;-&gt; Sweet88Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||07-04-2000||04:08 PM||||If you paid $200 for the whole car, I am assuming its either a wrecked car or an old car with a tired engine. You are tight on money.<P>There ain't much you can do to a tired 3.0L engine to juice it up that don't cost money.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I'm not familiar with the 3.0L Buick engine, but there will probably be lots of things that will be needed to do to get it to fit in a Fiero and mesh with your current transmission.  You'll need to do your homework as to engine mount position, starter position, exhaust manifold, axels, transmission bolt hole patterns (flex plate for automatic, clutch if its manual.<P>You should have saved the $200 for a 3.1 rebuild kit for your current 2.8.  My $0.02 worth.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000003||HYPTNOTiSE||07-04-2000||04:37 PM||||i think, not 100% positive, i looked at a 3.0 in a grand am, and it looks like part of the 3.3 and 3.8 liter engines.<P>who knows?<P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||07-06-2000||12:02 AM||||The 3.0-liter Buick engine is a 90-degree engine and your 2.8 is a 60-degree engine. The fiero stuff won't fit the Buick engine. I think that Buick engine is 140 HP and your 2.8 is 140 HP so why a Buick 3.0 liter engine? Your not gaining anything but a crappy .2 liters increase in displacment.||||reg||1
